Worksheet:

**F1 Core loop**: S global state; R() reads/writes S.rngState (no Math.random found); runTurn() calls stormPhase→production→needsPhase→eventsPhase→caravanPhase→checkEnd in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 Map**: genMap(seed) builds 64-tile grid via mkRng; tryBuild checks d.terr.includes(s.map[i]); adjCount() feeds condenser/greenhouse/forge output multipliers. Score 2.

**F3 Economy**: soil→food (greenhouse spends soil/water), ore→metal (forge), metal→parts (workshop); caps() enforced via addRes() clamp+overflow log. Score 2.

**F4 Population**: colonist objects {skill,fatigue,morale,b}; workerMult() reads c.skill (job-matched) and c.fatigue (exhausted×0.5) in production(). Score 2.

**F5 Needs**: needsPhase() subtracts pop food/water, sets foodShort/waterShort → dm morale delta; recovery dm=2+bonuses when no shortage. Score 2.

**F6 Research**: 10 nodes, tryResearch enforces node.req.every(has), spend(cost); each effect read elsewhere (has(s,"filters") in condenser, has(s,"shield") in stormPhase mit, etc). Score 2.

**F7 Events**: 12 EVENTS entries; weighted roll in eventsPhase (roll-=e.w loop); 6 events with 2-3 choices mutating state differently; s.cds[id]=EVENT_COOLDOWN checked in pool filter. Score 2.

**F8 Trade**: priceOf() uses s.res[g]/cap scarcity and s.drift[g] (random-walked in caravanPhase); cv.inv[g] limited stock; tradeDeal handles buy/sell both. Score 2.

**F9 Hazard**: stormPhase() fires turn%8===0, sev=1+floor(turn/20); production() halves output at hp<50, disables at hp<=0; shield research + wall building reduce mit; tryRepair spends parts/metal+labor. Score 2.

**F10 Save/load**: exportSave() JSON.stringify(stripUi(S)) into textarea; importSave() JSON.parse + required-field validation, returns error string shown in #saveerr. Score 2.

**F11 End conditions**: checkEnd() win (turn>=60,pop>=12,!shortage) and lose (colonists.length===0) both reachable; score() combines pop/research/turns/stockVal; renderModal() draws summary table. Score 2.

**F12 UI**: switchTab() wired to #tabs buttons; log entries carry `T${e.t}`; extensive title= tooltips explaining formulas; keydown listener for Space/1-5; @media(max-width:420px) layout rules. Score 2.

**F13 Dev panel**: runTests() asserts real invariants (storm schedule, prereqs, save round-trip hash, starvation departures); runBench() runs 200 headless greedyTurn() turns and prints stateHash(). Score 2.

**G1**: has(s,"filters")/"bore"/"turbine"/"drip" read directly inside production() multiplier lines, applied every turn, visible in b.note. Score 4.

**G2**: needsPhase() shortfall sets foodShort/waterShort → dm morale change → workerMult() reads c.morale (<40 ×0.7, 0 refuse) next production() call. Score 4.

**G3**: stormPhase() lowers b.hp → production() checks b.hp<50/<=0 for reduced/disabled output → tryRepair() spends parts+metal+idle labor, resets hp=100. Score 4.

**G4**: priceOf() = BASE_PRICE×drift[g]×scarcity(s.res[g]/cap); drift[g] random-walked every turn in caravanPhase(). Score 4.

**G5**: refugees choices call addColonist()/spend()/morale mutation; sickness choices spend(parts)/set fatigue=100/morale delta — all real state writes, not just logMsg. Score 4.

